          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -12 \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -12 \\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 \\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=-4\\\\ 0x+0y &=-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-4$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-4,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution.",
